  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3487 (head e30244c56), which fixes #3443 for picked contours.\n\n## What happens\nPR #3487 makes a picked contour refuse when a required section cannot be read. The whole-model contour paths (`contour_whole.rs:277`, `contour_whole_reach.rs:100`) still stop the ring at that level and write the note \"the part is solid below it\". The note is not true: the section was not readable.\n\nThe second half of \"Done means\" in #3443 (\"never reported as only a note\") is not met for whole-model contours.\n\n## Wanted\n- Decide the behaviour for the whole-model contour: refuse, or mark the operation \"incomplete\" with a true message. Record the decision.\n- Pin it with a test in `crates/motion/tests/`.\n\n## Also seen\n- The fixture `crates/motion/tests/contour_outside_floor/fixtures/sign_plate_3443.json` is 1.29 MB. A smaller fixture that shows the same fault is wanted.\n- The cause of the section failure on the sign plate, and its long run time for rings inside the hull, is not fixed.\n",
